Cs2AgBiBr6,TiO2,Spiro-OMeTAD,2.08,NOT_STATED,NOT_STATED,10.1038/s41598-025-02203-8,"Raj, A., Kumar, M., Singh, D.V. et al. Physical parameter optimization and band alignment approach for efficiency improvement in Cs2AgBiBr6 based lead-free perovskite solar cells, Scientific Reports (Nature, open access, 2025)",DFT (WIEN2k) + SCAPS-1D,"The DFT revealed the optimized band gap of 2.08 eV of Cs2AgBiBr6. The PSCs was designed with cell configurations of FTO/TiO2/Cs2AgBiBr6/Spiro-OMeTAD/Au and superior PCE of 6.68% was achieved."
Cs2AgBiBr6,NOT_SPECIFIED,Cu2O,2.08,NOT_STATED,NOT_STATED,10.1038/s41598-025-02203-8,"Raj, A., Kumar, M., Singh, D.V. et al. Physical parameter optimization and band alignment approach for efficiency improvement in Cs2AgBiBr6 based lead-free perovskite solar cells, Scientific Reports (Nature, open access, 2025)",DFT + SCAPS-1D,"PSCs were designed in SCAPS simulation software with cell configuration of FTO/TiO2/Cs2AgBiBr6/HTLs (CuI, CuSCN, Cu2O, Spiro-OMeTAD)/Au... The Cu2O HTL based PSCs experienced lower defects at interfacial point due to suitable band alignment with Cs2AgBiBr6 perovskite absorber. The PSCs exhibited maximum device efficiency of 7.60%, 6.28%, 5.56%, and 5.68% for Cu2O, CuSCN, CuI and spiro-OMeTAD based PSCs."
